id: pm-ngofg9
title: "Event-driven MCP agentic messaging: authenticated webhooks and channels compose with Tasks, subscriptions, progress, steering, and cancellation without polling"
description: "Define the next event-driven layer above the 2026-07-28 Tasks and subscriptions baseline so long-running agents can receive server events, stream results, and steer work without hidden sessions or client polling. Delivery semantics, authorization, replay, backpressure, cancellation, and durable pm history are SDK-owned contracts."
type: Feature
status: open
priority: 2
tags[7]: agentic-messaging,"area:mcp","area:sdk",channels,events,long-running,webhooks
created_at: "2026-08-28T20:22:14.270Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-28T20:58:31.045Z"
deadline: "2027-03-31T00:00:00.000Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 900
acceptance_criteria: Webhook and channel capabilities are explicitly discovered and negotiated; delivery identity ordering retry replay deduplication retention and terminal semantics are specified; Tasks subscriptions progress steering cancellation and MRTR share one lifecycle model; authorization binds every endpoint channel and event to an audience and least privilege; the public SDK owns an event provider and durable cursor contracts; real transports plus disconnect flood replay and forgery negative controls pass; clients can complete the canonical long-running journey without polling
parent: pm-opw1l3
risk: high
confidence: medium
